<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham van Peere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1627">1627</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham van Peere was a merchant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Vlissingen</a> in Zeeland who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colony of Berbice in present-day Guyana. In 1627 he received a charter from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> to settle the Berbice river, and his family held the colony as a private patroonship for decades, beginning with a trading post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-nassau-gold-coast">Fort Nassau</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1627 the Zeeland merchant <b>Abraham van Peere</b> received a charter from the Dutch West India Company to settle the Berbice river.</blockquote><a href="/state/berbice">Berbice</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Vlissingen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/netherlands">the Netherlands</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.45,3.58&amp;year=1627" aria-label="Vlissingen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4631 382 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Abraham van Peere"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5081 652h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5081 652h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.45,3.58&amp;year=1627">What was here in 1627? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
